{"type":"click","text":"C\n    \n      Foundation First, Remotes in Waves\n      Build the Nx scaffold + shared libs first, then build remotes in parallel waves.\n      Phase 1: Nx workspace, shell app, shared libs (state, API, SSE, design system, types). Phase 2: Build all 4 remotes in parallel against the shared contracts. Phase 3: Integration, Tauri hookup, parity verification. No hybrid — pure Angular, but structured for parallel team execution.\n\n      \n        \n          Pros\n          \n            Clean architecture — no migration bridges\n            Shared contracts defined first — teams can work independently\n            Parallel remote development (4 teams/tracks at once)\n            Fastest path to full parity with multi-team model\n          \n        \n        \n          Cons\n          \n            Foundation phase blocks all remote work (must be solid)\n            Still a full rewrite — React app frozen during build\n            Shared lib API may need revision once remotes start building\n          \n        \n      \n      \n        ⟵ RECOMMENDED  \n        Timeline: Foundation → Parallel remotes → Integration → Switch","choice":"c","id":null,"timestamp":1774379425468}
